@@ -3,3 +3,17 @@
 A small TypeScript library, with no runtime dependency, of building blocks for our services that store,
 exchange and update JSON: configuration files, API payloads and stored records. It is imported by the
 other projects of the team, so its behaviour must follow the published standards it implements.
+
+## JSON Pointer
+
+`resolvePointer(document, pointer)` resolves a value in a JSON document using an
+[RFC 6901 JSON Pointer](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6901). It returns the
+referenced value, including `null` and other falsy values, and throws when the
+pointer is malformed or does not identify a value.
+
+```ts
+import { resolvePointer } from "json-toolkit";
+
+const document = { services: [{ name: "api" }] };
+const name = resolvePointer(document, "/services/0/name"); // "api"
+```
